TEXT -64 240 Left 5 ;Ferroresonanz occure if:\nSwitcher1 is closed first\nTransformer has residual flux and delta wiring at primary side\nCable has 20km length (capacity)
TEXT -64 344 Left 5 ;You can see that at closing the switcher of phase1 at primary side\nthe voltages of phase2,3 goes very high (1.6MV vs\n326kV nominal = 4x till 5x nominal voltage level)\nThe secondary voltage at phase1 gets also high\n(250kV vs 98kV)\nAt t=1s the second and third switcher (phase2,3)\non the primary side get closed.\nNow the voltage levels begin to go to their nominal values again
TEXT 256 88 Left 2 ;Residual max. flux at t=20ms (switching time)
TEXT 272 200 Left 2 ;Due to the residual flux\nThe transformer start saturated
